00:33:31.390 --> 00:33:44.170
<v Griffin Hansbury>I said, no. It doesn't bother me. Because up until now, I used to be a woman. We never had a second date.
<v Griffin Hansbury>我说，不。这不困扰我。因为直到现在，我过去曾是个女人。我们再也没约会过第二次。

00:33:44.170 --> 00:33:55.210
<v Griffin Hansbury>My friend Ethan doesn't have these problems. Unlike the rest of us, he's had absolutely no fear of The Crying Game. When I ask him how he can be so confident, he just shrugs his shoulders. It never occurs to him to be afraid.
<v Griffin Hansbury>我的朋友伊桑（Ethan）没有这些问题。不像我们其他人，他完全没有对《哭泣游戏》的恐惧。当我问他为什么能这么自信时，他只是耸耸肩。他从来没想过要害怕。

00:33:55.210 --> 00:34:18.370
<v Griffin Hansbury>An easy-going and good-looking, dance club DJ with mutton-chop sideburns and armloads of tattoos, Ethan's a babe magnet. In his glove compartment, he keeps a spare toothbrush and a clean pair of boxer shorts. That's confidence. Ethan can pick up a woman in a bar, tell her about his past, and go home with her the same night-- no big deal. Here's an example of the kind of story he tells.
